.policy "ruff-d105-undocumented-magic-method" revision 2
.description "Add a docstring to each magic method of a public class, describing what the operation does and returns."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D105 (pydocstyle): a dunder method of a public class with no docstring, other than `__init__` (D107),
// `__new__` and `__call__` (D102). Not checked: `@overload`/`@override` methods, defs decorated with a
// `pydocstyle.ignore-decorators` entry, and `.pyi` stubs.
//   class C:
//       """Doc."""
//       def __eq__(self, o): …   ← D105 at `__eq__`
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D105(at: node, x: symbol) code "D105"
    "Add a docstring to magic method `{x}` describing its behavior, arguments and return value."
    suppress ruff "D105"
D105(nm, x) :- doc_missing(_, "method", nm, x), dunder(x), x != "__init__", x != "__new__", x != "__call__".